  "description": "ASIMP is an Ansible-powered security framework that measures, hardens, and re-measures Linux systems against CIS and Lynis compliance benchmarks.\nASIMP (Ansible System Integrity Management Platform) is an open-source, Ansible-powered framework for automated Linux security hardening, compliance auditing, and system integrity monitoring. It is designed for system administrators, security engineers, and DevOps teams who manage Linux fleets and need a repeatable, evidence-based process for bringing hosts into compliance with industry security benchmarks — without sacrificing visibility or control over what changes are made."
